// ## 8. Recommended same-commit repairs (orchestrator lane)

// A single same-commit patch can close most of these:

// 1. **Refresh the 4 audit verdicts** to 2026-09-10. file-law
//    moves from "PASS on 256-line cap" to "FAIL on 256-line
//    cap" (index.html is 1890). truth-drift moves from
//    "PASS" to "STALE — see 2026-09-10 cross-ref audit".
//    security and spa-drag stay PASS at the verdict level
//    but get a "refreshed 2026-09-10" stamp.
// 2. **Regenerate pulled/<repo>.oot × 11** to current tags.
//    This is the same pull workflow that produced
//    pulled/daily_audit_2026-09-10.oot; it lives in the
//    openOODA/.github/docs/ regeneration chain (per
//    pulled/ANCHOR.oo).
// 3. **Split index.html** into multiple ≤ 256-line files.
//    The SPA is the natural target (route + theme + dogfight
//    are already split; index.html is the static home
//    shell + nav + install box). Per file-law.oot:42
//    "do not add a second stylesheet or a new .js file
//    except to split an over-cap file" — this is the
//    exception that allows the split.
// 4. **Bump sitemap.xml lastmod** to 2026-09-10.

// Recommended order: (3) split index.html FIRST (so file-law
// can be re-derived as PASS); (2) regen pulled; (1) refresh
// 4 audits; (4) bump sitemap. One commit, one push, one
// auto-release.

